&lt;p&gt;Konrad is a global leader in AI and digital innovation consulting. We help the world’s top businesses and brands succeed in the AI era. We are dedicated to solving complex business problems for our global clients with creative, forward-thinking solutions and AI-enabled products. Our employees enjoy a culture built on innovation and a commitment to creating best-in-class, AI-driven digital products used by hundreds of millions of consumers around the world. We hire exceptionally smart, analytical, and hardworking people who are lifelong learners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Consultant on our Strategy team, you will work in a multifaceted role with global organizations as they embrace digital transformation and innovate for the AI era. Collaborating closely with our Design and Technology teams, you will help solve complex business problems by creating smart, intuitive, and human-centered experiences. You will support senior team members on our projects as you build your consulting experience, identifying how emerging technologies like AI can be leveraged to build best-in-class digital products and reshape our clients&#39; capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the broader team in understanding our clients&#39; business models, goals, and competitive pressures, recognizing where AI and emerging tech can materially change how they perform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the creation of AI-forward digital solutions and target-state operating models for a variety of clients and industries, contributing to AI strategy and product strategy work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather information on our clients&#39; business processes, critical success factors, and market standing through stakeholder interviews and research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our advisory work on digital transformation, including exploring how AI is reshaping intelligent products, customer experiences, and competitive dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with our Design and Technology teams to bridge the gap between business strategy and elegant, human-centered user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and participate in user experience design thinking workshops, technology architecture sessions, and project planning activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and author presentations, documentation, Request for Proposal (RFP) responses, and other collateral to a standard expected by a senior audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the evolving AI, digital, and product innovation landscape, sharing insights that strengthen our internal expertise and client deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in any discipline or equivalent professional experience; we hire from business, engineering, math, statistics, science, economics, and beyond, and prior consulting experience is not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in consulting, user experience, product management, and/or engineering is a strong asset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrable passion for and understanding of great user experiences, product innovation, and the rapidly evolving AI technology landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to help structure complex, ambiguous business problems and communicate a clear, analytical point of view&lt;/li&gt;
